{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/38192-playing-in-stygia-s-past","id":38192,"title":"Playing in Stygia's Past","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-28T00:51:21-08:00","id":38192,"title":"Playing in Stygia's Past","content":"(I'm determined to force the opening of a Wraith subforum.)<br /> <br /> I've been working on gathering notes on the Great Maelstroms, and the idea hit me of playing during those time periods. The First Great Maelstrom was the result of the sacking of Rome and led to Stygia being overrun by Spectres; the Second Great Maelstrom was the result of the Black Plague and resulted in the Spectres being successfully held back by the early Legions. The Third Great Maelstrom came as the result of the Spanish conquest of Mesoamerica (and the subsequent destruction of the Flayed Lands), and led to Stygia becoming an 'island' inside the Tempest. The Fourth we know well (detailed in Wraith: The Great War) and the Fifth was a result of the bloodshed of World War 2, which led to Charon's apparent destruction. The Sixth destroys the underworld as we know it, creates the Stormwall, and starts the Spectral civil war.<br /> <br /> I'm not entirely sure where I'm going with this, other than as a suggestion of future stretch goals or a fan project. These time periods (the fall of Rome, the Middle Ages, the conquest of the Americas, the World Wars, and the biggest cosmological event in the cWoD) all make fantastic settings that allow troupes to see Stygia from many different views. Before the Third, you still have the Guilds being sanctioned and a less isolated Stygia, and after the Sixth, you practically have a new game!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-28T05:31:57-08:00","id":38253,"title":"","content":"I'm actually really curious what it was like at the beginning of Charon's days, and before it. And what about way before like the ancient days of Egypt and Sumer?<br /> <br /> And I'm quite curious about what everything was like in the Dark Ages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-28T10:35:21-08:00","id":38336,"title":"","content":"I completely agree. It would be great to see the other maelstroms and early history of the empire given proper detail/special rules similar to the great war.<br /> <br /> Dark Ages wraith would be really interesting, its too bad we did not see more of it in the original run. Egypt in particular would be cool to learn more about (a civilization with so well developed funerary rituals must breed some fearsome wraiths). I would also like to learn more about Stygia's involvement/presence in Egypt (past and present).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The Mercy of Order is Justice&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1391-aeoris","name":"Aeoris","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-28T16:55:29-08:00","id":38493,"title":"","content":"An idea that sprang to mind that isn't necessarily tied to a Great Maelstrom: Stygia claims domain over all wraiths, but only really holds positions tied to Europe, North America, and places colonized by European powers. This has led to struggles in the past - Indian and African wraiths who died in the first World War ended up in Stygian territory instead of their respective Dark Kingdoms - but one somewhat recent incident springs to mind that hasn't been discussed. The Vietnam War was a bloody debacle that cost over 50,000 American lives and many more Vietnamese.<br /> <br /> I imagine many of the American dead would become wraiths upon death; they were drafted right out of high school and flown halfway around the world to die traumatic deaths. Death in Vietnam would send them to the Dark Kingdom of Jade, and I can't imagine they would be well-treated on the other side. The Dark Kingdom of Jade has never gotten along well with Stygia, and there is little chance of getting those souls back peacefully.<br /> <br /> In other words, Wraith deserves another brutal, depressing setting: Vietnam War Wraith. Rather than the all-out war of The Great War (or the conflict in Ends Of Empire), you have secret infiltration from Stygia into the Yellow Springs, and a resistance formed by the American dead who are now essentially POWs. Death by all manner of booby traps would send many American dead straight to Oblivion upon their passing, so I imagine a fair deal of chaos (akin to a mini-Great Maelstrom) in the Yellow Springs at the time.<br /> <br /> It's not gonna be pretty.<br /> <br /> (A potentially interesting subversion; now the Americans are the guerillas against an overwhelming, organized force.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":281,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","user":"atamajakki","date":". 12-28-2013, 08:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-28T17:37:36-08:00","id":38505,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>They took you after you graduated and threw you halfway around the world to fight a war you didn\u2019t believe in. Your death came suddenly; your foot snagged a tripwire in the jungle and it was lights out. You feel cheated; your band never had the chance to hit it big, and you never got to marry your high school sweetheart.</i></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>That\u2019s the least of your worries right now. You\u2019re dead, but this sure as hell isn\u2019t Heaven. This afterlife feels an awful lot like enemy territory, and you\u2019re outnumbered; the boys from your squad against every Charlie to ever die. The odds are looking slim, but you\u2019re not going down without a fight.<br /> <br /> We gotta get out of this place.</i></span></span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-28T18:07:12-08:00","id":38522,"title":"","content":"Actually if I remember correctly in the two Dark Kingdom of Jade books they talk about Americans killed in Vietnam though it's been a long time since I've read those ones. I'll have to double check.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-28T20:09:59-08:00","id":38553,"title":"","content":"Yeah I was right, both books talk about them. Officially the Dark Kingdoms of Iron and Jade had an agreement that wraiths belong to the Kingdom of the place they were born in so an American would go to Stygia, a Vietnamese would go to the Kingdom of Jade. In reality... well few wraiths born in Korean and Vietnamese Wars made it to Stygia, most were forced into the Imperial Army where they were stuck in the lowest positions possible and forbidden from resolving their Passions. But a number of them fled the Army and formed a resistance group, the Lost Legion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-28T20:25:03-08:00","id":38560,"title":"","content":"Something I find to be interesting is the numbering scheme. The Great Maelstroms are recorded <i>after</i> the formation of Stygia, who knows how many there were before the city's founding? Was there a Great Maelstrom when the dinosaurs were wiped out? What happened, how did it affect the Underworld? Or was the Underworld uninhabited, nothing but sleeping Malfeans in the Labyrinth?<br /> <br /> And I believe that <i>Mummy: the Resurrection</i> touched on the ancient Egyptian Underworld in their creation myth. I recall some crossover in the whole Dark Umbra/Underworld thing. Piecing together information from <i>M:tR</i> and the Ferryman's chapter from Ends of Empire might be an interesting place to start.<br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-29T16:26:38-08:00","id":38947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/38192-playing-in-stygia-s-past?p=38560#post38560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Was there a Great Maelstrom when the dinosaurs were wiped out? What happened, how did it affect the Underworld? Or was the Underworld uninhabited, nothing but sleeping Malfeans in the Labyrinth?</div> </div> </div> </div>This isn't answered specifically, but judging by the fact that there are animal ghosts in the DK of Ivory, it makes sense that there were dinoghosts.That said, there is a significant difference between dinosaurs and we Apes. Then again, there are weredinosaurs, so who knows? I don't see it causing a Great Maelstrom in any event, however.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/426-big-brother","name":"Big Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar426_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-29T16:30:58-08:00","id":38954,"title":"","content":"I'm guessing by the time of the Wonder Work(the Meteor) and now the Underworld we have in the present is probably a different place. We could have easily have had multiple underworlds in the meantime. Or maybe if you dig in the right Place you can find Ruins of a lost age of Dinosaur Kings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-29T21:09:52-08:00","id":39098,"title":"","content":"On the Vietnam material; I read the two Dark Kingdom of Jade books, and you were right. A Vietnam veteran named Colonel Roth leads the wraiths of American dead from the Pacific Theater in WW2, the Korean War, and the Vietnam War, all in a guerilla resistance called the Lost Legion. They're all insanely patriotic, and believe that they will go to Heaven if the Emperor of the Dark Kingdom of Jade is destroyed. They reject the Hierarchy as having abandoned them, but need allies in order to continue their fight. <br /> <br /> Ideally, a Vietnam War setting would show the early Lost Legion as not quite as fanatical and more dedicated to survival.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-30T22:58:51-08:00","id":39810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/38192-playing-in-stygia-s-past?p=39098#post39098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the Vietnam material; I read the two Dark Kingdom of Jade books, and you were right. A Vietnam veteran named Colonel Roth leads the wraiths of American dead from the Pacific Theater in WW2, the Korean War, and the Vietnam War, all in a guerilla resistance called the Lost Legion. They're all insanely patriotic, and believe that they will go to Heaven if the Emperor of the Dark Kingdom of Jade is destroyed. They reject the Hierarchy as having abandoned them, but need allies in order to continue their fight.<br /> <br /> Ideally, a Vietnam War setting would show the early Lost Legion as not quite as fanatical and more dedicated to survival.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait this is where the lost Legion Came From?! I remember the latest info on them came from Umbra Revised, where they wound up in the Abyss having been blasted to true lost-ness by the Maelstrom!<br /> <br /> <br /> But yeah one thing to consider is Vietnam's native Wraiths are oppressed by the Imperial Wraiths of China, so their may be a good deal of middle ground for foreign Wraiths lost there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-30T23:28:27-08:00","id":39828,"title":"","content":"I want to see the First and Third Great Maelstrom time periods explored. The first gives us the Wraiths of Rome and her territories (I'm a huge fan of Rome, I'm sorry) and you'd get to see Stygia in its infancy, when Charon was fully imperator in the eyes of the people; struggling through the fall of Stygia to the Spectres would be brutal, and I'd love nothing more than to see the massive cultural variety of the Empire. Plus, details on potential Dark Kingdoms for Egypt and the barbarians of Gaul, Germany, and Britain.<br /> <br /> The Third Great Maelstrom brings the disbanding of the Guilds (so they would be a greater power than what we're used to seeing) and a cultural clash with the Dark Kingdoms of the Americas, which scarcely exist in modern nights. It would be wonderful to see an equally powerful empire of the dead in decline, but still a threat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-30T23:29:57-08:00","id":39829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/38192-playing-in-stygia-s-past?p=39810#post39810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wait this is where the lost Legion Came From?! I remember the latest info on them came from Umbra Revised, where they wound up in the Abyss having been blasted to true lost-ness by the Maelstrom!<br /> <br /> <br /> But yeah one thing to consider is Vietnam's native Wraiths are oppressed by the Imperial Wraiths of China, so their may be a good deal of middle ground for foreign Wraiths lost there.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could very well see an unlikely alliance of the Lost Legion and the wraiths of Vietnam and Japan (was Korea oppressed too?) against the emperor of the Dark Kingdom of Jade.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-30T23:42:01-08:00","id":39834,"title":"","content":"I like to think the Rome Era Stygia is a time when the Underworld is finally being tamed, but you still have Wraiths around from a few centuries ago when Hekatonhires and true gigantic horrors regularly wandered the Tempest and possibly even the Shadowlands.<br /> <br /> <br /> And yeah the Dark Kingdom of Jade basically subjugated all of Asia, minus Russia and India. He realized he could have unprecedented control and Stability of the Chinese Dead if he made all other Controlled territories 2nd class citizens and therefore subject to Slavery and Soul Forging-err Jade Forging.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-31T00:39:23-08:00","id":39844,"title":"","content":"Can someone check my timeline?<br /> <span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The First Great Maelstrom: Charon, one of the Ferrymen, believes the increasing numbers of the dead need structure in order to find Transcendence. He founds Stygia, the Dark Kingdom of Iron, as a means for wraiths to find their way to their ultimate reward. When Rome falls, the chaos and death tears open a Great Maelstrom; Stygia is sacked by Spectres, and it takes many years for it to be rebuilt.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The Second Great Maelstrom: The Black Plague sweeps across Europe, killing millions in just a handful of years. Stygia, slowly rebuilt since the time of Rome, enjoys a swell in citizens. The massive death toll causes another Great Maelstrom; Spectres once again lay siege to the Dark Kingdom of Iron, but are successfully repelled by the Legions.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The Third Great Maelstrom: Charon officially disavows the Guilds, wary of their increasing power. In the Skinlands, the Spanish conquer the Americas, nearly wiping out the natives. A similar war envelops the lands of the dead, with Stygia seeking to claim the Americas; the twin wars begin another Great Maelstrom. The Spaniards and the Stygians win their wars, but the chaos stirs the Tempest up around the Isle of Sorrow, cutting off easy access to it through the Tempest.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The Fourth Great Maelstrom: Charon disappears. The War to End All Wars turns all of Europe into a battlefield; the dead cross over in greater numbers than ever before. The death of so many millions in such a violent manner releases a Great Maelstrom. Lacking a clear leader, the Smiling Lord of the Grim Legion makes a big for power; civil war engulfs the Dark Kingdom of Iron, even as Spectres pound on the gates. Stygia survives, though heavily battered.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The Fifth Great Maelstrom: The Second World War once again soaks Europe and the Pacific in blood. Industrialized genocide brings enough despair to tear open a new Great Maelstrom, with the Spectres led by a fearsome creature known as Gorool. Charon reappears to challenge Gorool; both plunge into a great gulf and are assumed lost. Stygia once again weathers the storm, at great cost.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The Sixth Great Maelstrom: The Dark Kingdom of Jade, working alongside the traitorous Smiling Lord, declares war on Stygia. The war is brutal; an unknown event deep within the Tempest pushes the madness into a full Great Maelstrom. The Dark Kingdom of Jade is repelled, though the Spectres remain. Charon returns to hold off the horde, but quickly Transcends. The Dark Kingdom of Iron falls, and the chaos that comes in the wake only strengthens the Maelstrom. A powerful Malfean known as Grandmother awakens.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Post-Sixth Great Maelstrom: The Maelstrom does not abate, rendering the Shadowlands nearly uninhabitable due to a constant rain of shards and debris. Spectres roam freely, but appear to fight among themselves. Many wraiths are blown through the Shroud into the Skinlands; others are blown <i>into</i> the Shroud, strengthening it until it becomes the nearly impassable Stormwall. Most Necropoli are presumed lost, but may survive and city-states under siege.</span></span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-31T01:38:23-08:00","id":39859,"title":"","content":"Its also worth Noting after the 6th Great Maelstrom we have an Influx of two types of beings who even a single member of could support a burgeoning Ghost Empire. Mummies and Demons.<br /> <br /> <br /> But this makes me think the war between the Dark Kingdom of Obsidian/Flayed Lands and Stygia probably resulted in Stygia discovering/plundering an innumerable amount of potent Artifacts/Relics. I wonder what are some examples of Items stolen from the lands of the Jaguar gods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-31T13:25:49-08:00","id":40132,"title":"","content":"<u>Timeline</u><br /> Stygia founded as a Republic.<br /> Rise of the Renegades.<br /> Fishers appear.<br /> \u2022 First Great Maelstrom: 476 AD, triggered by the sacking of Rome. Stygia falls.<br /> Stygia rebuilt. Hierarchy founded; Guilds established. <br /> \u2022 Second Great Maelstrom: 1347 AD, triggered by the Black Plague.<br /> Fishers purged. Rise of the Heretics. <br /> \u2022 Third Great Maelstrom: 1598 AD, triggered by the Siege of Stygia, the Breaking of the Guilds, and war with the Dark Kingdom of Obsidian. <br /> The first Necropolis is founded in London.<br /> \u2022 Fourth Great Maelstrom: 1918 AD, triggered by World War I.<br /> \u2022 Fifth Great Maelstrom: 1945 AD, triggered by World War II\u2019s nukes. <br /> Gorool appears; Charon disappears. <br /> \u2022 Sixth Great Maelstrom: 1999 AD, triggered by the Week of Nightmares. <br /> <br /> It\u2019s interesting that the Republic of Stygia was concurrent with the Roman Empire as well as the Roman Republic, and did not fall until the Roman Empire fell. <br /> <br /> Personally, I\u2019d like to see a <b>Dark Ages: Wraith</b> supplement, set in the early days of the Hierarchy with the Guilds still active and traffic with the Far Shores commonplace, and with the Fishers being the Shadowlands\u2019 counterpart to the Catholic Church and being major players in Stygia. Set it prior to the Second Great Maelstrom, and concurrent with the new Dark Ages line.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-31T18:11:32-08:00","id":40274,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/38192-playing-in-stygia-s-past?p=40132#post40132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Sixth Great Maelstrom: 1999 AD, triggered by the Week of Nightmares.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was under the impression that the Smiling Lord going all Hiroshima on Enoch is what kicked off the 6GM... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-31T19:16:18-08:00","id":40296,"title":"","content":"That's part of it. Two separate relic nukes* were detonated at the same time though at different places and for different reasons. One was the destruction of Enoch as you mentioned, the other was done by a VE, Xerxes Jones got into the Labyrinth and detonated his nuke in the mouth of Oblivion as part of an experiment. The events of the Week of Nightmares, namely the weapons the Technocracy used against Zapathasura weakened things in the Underworld (and the Umbra) amplifying the later effects of the relic nukes detonating.<br /> <br /> *They may have been the relics of Fat Man and Little Boy but I can't remember.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-31T19:16:50-08:00","id":40297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nazfool</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/38192-playing-in-stygia-s-past?p=40274#post40274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"> I was under the impression that the Smiling Lord going all Hiroshima on Enoch is what kicked off the 6GM... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></span></div> </div> </div> </div> The 6GM is a combination on the was between Iron and Jade, plus the nuke going off at the mouth of Oblivion. I wouldn't mind seeing that retconned; a curious Technocrat ending Wraith leaves a bad taste in my mouth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-31T19:26:39-08:00","id":40299,"title":"","content":"Well technically he was working with the Orphic Circle, a group of humans, mages, vampires and other obsessed with the nature of death. And they were the ones who gave Jones the nuke.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-31T22:46:31-08:00","id":40365,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/38192-playing-in-stygia-s-past?p=40297#post40297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I wouldn't mind seeing that retconned; a curious Technocrat ending Wraith leaves a bad taste in my mouth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I like the idea of the Great Maelstroms being caused by atrocities in the Skinlands (by mundane meatbags) or horrible crap going on in the Underworld (by the ectoplasmic living impaired).<br /> <br /> Still, I\u2019m not terribly worried about ret-con. Assuming Wr20 goes the \u201cmetaplot-agnostic\u201d route of the prior 20<sup>th</sup> anniversary additions, the Sixth Great Maelstrom can be caused by Stygian nukes, Balefire nukes, the resurgence of wyrm-tainted weregerbils, or Cain farting. <br /> <br /> This is why tabletop rpgs are my favorite source of entertainment. You and your troupe are writing the stories. It\u2019s you world. You don\u2019t have to worry about why Klingons have brow-ridges, how Darth Vader became a Sith Lord, why Blood Elves are part of the Horde, or a host of other pieces of ret-con.<br /> <br /> If you\u2019d like, I can pen this in the <i>Derpanomicon: Nazfool\u2019s Erroneous Compendium of Unofficial Miscellanea:</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">And lo! It came to pass that the Smiling Lord launched a nuke at some Underworld island that was randomly inhabited by vampires, who got done blown up. And this causes the Sixth Great Maelstrom why not. </span><br /> <br /> [This ret-con stuff is easy. No wonder George Lucas was always f\u2019ing with movies when the whim struck him.] </span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-01T08:11:56-08:00","id":40503,"title":"","content":"But it wasn't <i>just </i>Jones and his bomb, it was the combination of the two bombs, if only one had gone off the 6GM probably wouldn't have been as severe. In fact I vaguely recall reading somewhere that Jones's nuke may have actually gone off prematurely, triggered by the detonation of the first in Enoch. Given that nothing is written about Jones afterwords, strange given that he helped bring about the 6GM, it seems to imply that he was caught in the blast of his bomb which is strange as you'd think he would have gotten to a safe distance from the area before setting it off. Of course it could just be that he was caught in the emerging Maelstrom.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}